 # Dimension: D3 — 凹痕识别条件：3x3邻域多数色判定 (transform)
 # Change: 凹痕的（清洁后）3x3邻域中多数前景色为某一色时，该凹痕被认定为属于该色区域并触发变换... → 要求邻域全部为同一前景色（非多数）
 
-# Design analysis for the D3 variant
-# ----------------------------------
-# spec:
-#   source_task: None
-#   unchanged_core:
-#     grid: square, 20-30
-#     palette: black background, 2 non-black/non-teal foreground colors, teal mark color
-#     regions: 2-3 overlapping rectangles, simple occlusion
-#     cleanup: keep the original two-sweep local denoising
-#     transform_shape: every accepted dent still creates an opposite-color 3x3 patch with a teal center
-#   d3_change:
-#     original_recognition: a black cell was a dent if, after cleanup, one foreground color had a strict 3x3 majority with at least 5 cells
-#     new_recognition: keep the same minimum support (>=5 host cells), but replace "strict majority over the other color" with
-#       "all non-black cells in the cleaned 3x3 belong to one foreground color"
-#     practical_effect: dents deep inside one region still transform; dents whose 3x3 touches both foreground regions stay black
-#   behavior_trace:
-#     original_example:
-#       clean_3x3_counts: {host: 6, other: 2, black: 1}
-#       original_solver: accepted because 6 >= 5 and 6 > 2
-#       variant_solver: rejected because two foreground colors are present
-#     strict_example:
-#       clean_3x3_counts: {host: 7, other: 0, black: 2}
-#       original_solver: accepted
-#       variant_solver: also accepted because every non-black pixel has the same color
-#   complexity_calibration:
-#     concern: if the generator only places deep dents, the new rule becomes invisible because old/new outputs match
-#     fix: generate two dent classes
-#       1. strict dents: uniform cleaned 3x3, these transform
-#       2. mixed dents: host-majority but not host-uniform cleaned 3x3, these remain black
-#     visibility: mixed dents are kept few but guaranteed present so 2-4 examples are enough to see that interface-adjacent holes are not converted
-#   implicit_assumption_review:
-#     _clean_foreground:
-#       assumption: cleanup is independent from the dent-recognition rule
-#       status: still valid, so left unchanged
-#     _dent_centers:
-#       old assumption: choosing the max-count color is enough
-#       issue: with D3, a max-count host is not sufficient if the other foreground color also appears
-#       fix: explicitly test that exactly one foreground color appears in the cleaned 3x3 and that its count is at least 5
-#     output_stamping:
-#       assumption: every punched hole is transformed
-#       issue: no longer true because mixed dents must survive as black cells
-#       fix: generator output is built from the clean regions, then mixed dents are re-blackened after stamping transformed dents
-#   placement_legality:
-#     strict dents and mixed dents are both chosen with Chebyshev separation >= 3, so 3x3 effects stay readable
-#     mixed dents are chosen only from cells whose clean 3x3 already contains both foreground colors, so they are guaranteed non-transforming under D3
-#     transformed pairs are only expanded inside strict-uniform host regions, preventing ambiguous mixed pairs
-#   visual_cleanliness:
-#     black surviving dents are limited in count and kept away from transformed patches
-#     boundary noise generation is preserved, but oracle validation rejects any sample where noise would break the intended classification
-#   color_inference:
-#     no rule depends on color ids; colors only act as "host" vs "other"
-#     the visible cue for the rule is structural purity of the local neighborhood, not the numeric identity of a color
-
 from __future__ import annotations
 
 import random
@@ -64,6 +11,49 @@
 
 from arc_utils import Color
 
+# Design analysis for the D3 variant:
+# - Concrete behavior:
+#   The original task transformed a black dent when one foreground color merely
+#   dominated its cleaned 3x3 neighborhood. Here the trigger is stricter:
+#   a black cell is transformed only when all non-black cells in that cleaned
+#   3x3 belong to one foreground color, and there are still at least 5 such
+#   host cells. Mixed neighborhoods with both foreground colors stay black.
+#   Small trace:
+#     old: [a a a; a 0 b; a b b] -> host=a by 5>3, so it transformed.
+#     new: same neighborhood contains both a and b, so it does not transform.
+# - Complexity calibration:
+#   To make the difference visible, the generator creates both:
+#   1) deep interior dents whose 3x3 is uniformly one color and do transform;
+#   2) boundary-adjacent dents whose 3x3 contains both foreground colors and
